# Change Control

**Constitution:** §58–60, §63–64, §78–79

## STOP — Request Approval

- Destructive / irreversible DB changes
- Security or authorization bypass
- Breaking API without migration
- Data loss risk · tenant isolation risk
- New framework/runtime (React/Vue/Blazor/Electron) without ADR
- Removing protected functionality

## Delete Governance

Before delete: search repo, routes, APIs, tests, docs, DB usage, permissions.

Destructive delete on academic records: **FORBIDDEN** — use status + `effective_to`.

## Refactoring

Do not refactor unrelated code in feature tasks. Record unrelated debt as:

```text
TECHNICAL DEBT: {description}
```

## Protected Baselines

Phase gate reports (3.10.1, Enrollment A/B) — do not reopen without proven regression.
